 gray:"69 60 year old woman has poor controlled DM and history of HT for 10 years present with seizure for 5 mins. 1 week ago she had fever and dysuria for 3 days PE : T 38 C P110 bpm RR 20/min bp 120/80 mmHg. No sign of meningeal irritation What is a proper diagnostic investigation? — a. CT brain b. Lumbar puncture c. Capillary blood glucose",
 opts:["CT brain","Lumbar puncture","Capillary blood glucose","EEG","Urine culture"],ans:2,key:"C Capillary blood glucose"+KS,
